2025-05-01 02:16:52 - Thread-759 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage
• BADGES."class": identify gold badges (gold = 1)  
• BADGES."name": name of the badge to be grouped later  
• BADGES."date": moment the badge was awarded (micro‑seconds from Unix epoch)  
• BADGES."user_id": the owner of the badge, needed to join to USERS  
• USERS."id": primary key to match BADGES."user_id"  
• USERS."creation_date": account‑creation moment (same micro‑second epoch); will be subtracted from BADGES."date" to obtain the wait‑time in micro‑seconds, then converted to days  
Conditions that will be used
• BADGES."class" = 1  → keep only gold badges  
• QUALIFY or MIN() OVER (PARTITION BY "user_id")  → pick a user’s first gold badge  
• Aggregation: GROUP BY BADGE."name" to count users and AVG() the days difference  
• ORDER BY user‑count DESC FETCH 10  → top‑10 list  

Ten exploratory–to–final Snowflake SQL statements  
(Each query limited to 20 rows where meaningful; every identifier is double‑quoted.)

```sql
-- 1) Peek at a few gold‑badge awards
SELECT * 
FROM "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES"
WHERE "class" = 1 
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Distinct gold‑badge names and how many times they were awarded overall
SELECT "name", COUNT(*) AS "total_awarded"
FROM "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES"
WHERE "class" = 1
GROUP BY "name"
ORDER BY "total_awarded" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Join a sample of gold badges to their users to inspect the two time columns
SELECT b."user_id",
       b."name",
       b."date"          AS "badge_date",
       u."creation_date" AS "user_created"
FROM   "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES"  b
JOIN   "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."USERS"   u
       ON b."user_id" = u."id"
WHERE  b."class" = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) For each user, pull the first date they ever got a gold badge
SELECT "user_id",
       MIN("date") AS "first_gold_date"
FROM   "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES"
WHERE  "class" = 1
GROUP BY "user_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Same as #4 but include the badge name that was first, using QUALIFY
SELECT "user_id",
       "name",
       "date"
FROM   "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES"
WHERE  "class" = 1
QUALIFY "date" = MIN("date") OVER (PARTITION BY "user_id")
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Add the waiting‑time (in whole days, unadjusted) for a user’s first gold badge
SELECT b."user_id",
       b."name",
       b."date"                                            AS "badge_date",
       u."creation_date"                                   AS "user_created",
       (b."date" - u."creation_date") / 86400000000::FLOAT AS "days_to_badge"
FROM   "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES" b
JOIN   "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."USERS"  u
       ON b."user_id" = u."id"
WHERE  b."class" = 1
QUALIFY b."date" = MIN(b."date") OVER (PARTITION BY b."user_id")
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Aggregate: count how many users got each badge as their FIRST gold badge
SELECT b."name",
       COUNT(*) AS "users_first_gold"
FROM   "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES" b
WHERE  b."class" = 1
QUALIFY b."date" = MIN(b."date") OVER (PARTITION BY b."user_id")
GROUP BY b."name"
ORDER BY "users_first_gold" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Combine #6 and #7: also compute average days to earn that first gold badge
SELECT b."name",
       COUNT(*)                                                  AS "users_first_gold",
       AVG( (b."date" - u."creation_date") / 86400000000::FLOAT ) AS "avg_days_to_badge"
FROM   "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES" b
JOIN   "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."USERS"  u
       ON b."user_id" = u."id"
WHERE  b."class" = 1
QUALIFY b."date" = MIN(b."date") OVER (PARTITION BY b."user_id")
GROUP BY b."name"
ORDER BY "users_first_gold" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Same as #8 but retaining only badges earned by at least 100 users (example threshold)
SELECT b."name",
       COUNT(*)                                                  AS "users_first_gold",
       AVG( (b."date" - u."creation_date") / 86400000000::FLOAT ) AS "avg_days_to_badge"
FROM   "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES" b
JOIN   "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."USERS"  u
       ON b."user_id" = u."id"
WHERE  b."class" = 1
QUALIFY b."date" = MIN(b."date") OVER (PARTITION BY b."user_id")
GROUP BY b."name"
HAVING COUNT(*) >= 100
ORDER BY "users_first_gold" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL QUERY – top‑10 gold badges most commonly earned first,
--     with user count and average wait (days)
SELECT b."name"                                            AS "badge_name",
       COUNT(*)                                            AS "users_first_gold",
       AVG( (b."date" - u."creation_date") / 86400000000 ) AS "avg_days_to_badge"
FROM   "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES" b
JOIN   "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."USERS"  u
       ON b."user_id" = u."id"
WHERE  b."class" = 1
QUALIFY b."date" = MIN(b."date") OVER (PARTITION BY b."user_id")
GROUP BY b."name"
ORDER BY "users_first_gold" DESC
FETCH 10;
```

The final query (#10) will return:
• badge_name – the gold badge  
• users_first_gold – how many distinct users earned that badge as their very first gold badge  
• avg_days_to_badge – the average number of days from account creation to that badge (direct micro‑seconds difference divided by 86 400 000 000, no date‑format adjustments)
